      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, pursuant to section 414(h) of the Internal Revenue Code, employee\ncontributions to a public employer pension plan may be picked up on a pre-tax basis by the\npublic employer and excluded from an employee's federal gross income if the employer\nspecifies that the contributions, although designated as employee contributions to the plan, are\nbeing paid by the employer in lieu of contributions by the employee, and the employee cannot\nchoose to receive the amounts directly instead of having them paid by the employer; and",
